{% comment %}
  One accordion group in the collection sidebar.

  Extracted from xd-collection-grid so that a single Shopify filter can be
  rendered as SEVERAL groups. That is what `prefix` is for: Material, Player
  Level, Playing Style and Weight all arrive as one "Product tags" filter whose
  values read "Material: Carbon Fiber", "Level: Advanced" and so on, and this
  snippet renders the slice of them sharing one prefix, with the prefix stripped
  off the visible label.

  Why tags and not metafields, since the store has metafields for exactly these
  four things: Shopify INTERSECTS multiple values of a list-metafield filter.
  Ticking Carbon Fiber and Graphite asks for paddles that are both, which is no
  paddle at all - measured on this store: Graphite 3, Carbon Fiber 2, together
  0. Tag values are ORed, which is what multi-select has to mean. The metafields
  are still there and still correct; they are just not what the sidebar reads.

  Accepts:
    filter        - a collection filter (drop from collection.filters)
    prefix        - blank for a whole filter; otherwise the tag prefix to slice
    group_label   - accordion header text
    style         - price | swatch | rating | checkbox
    panel_id      - unique id for the collapse target
    show_count    - render each value's result count
    rating_suffix - text after the stars ("& Up")
    design_colours- comma list of colour handles main.css already paints
{% endcomment %}
{%- liquid
  assign design_colour_list = design_colours | split: ','
  assign separator = ': '

  # How many of this group's values are on. Price is one control rather than a
  # set, so its badge is 0 or 1.
  assign group_active = 0
  if filter.type == 'price_range'
    if filter.min_value.value != blank or filter.max_value.value != blank
      assign group_active = 1
    endif
  else
    for value in filter.active_values
      if prefix == blank
        assign group_active = group_active | plus: 1
      else
        assign value_prefix = value.label | split: separator | first
        if value_prefix == prefix
          assign group_active = group_active | plus: 1
        endif
      endif
    endfor
  endif
-%}
<div class="accordion-item" data-xd-group="{{ panel_id }}">
  <h2 class="accordion-header">
    <button
      class="accordion-button heading-font"
      type="button"
      data-bs-toggle="collapse"
      data-bs-target="#{{ panel_id }}"
    >
      {{- group_label | escape -}}
      {%- comment -%}
        Multi-select is only obvious if the group says how many of its values
        are on while it is collapsed.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <span class="xd-facet-group-count" data-xd-group-count {% if group_active == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}>
        {{- group_active -}}
      </span>
    </button>
  </h2>
  <div id="{{ panel_id }}" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" data-bs-parent="#filterAccordion">
    {%- case style -%}
      {%- when 'price' -%}
        <div class="accordion-body">
          <div class="price-values d-flex justify-content-between mb-2">
            <span data-xd-price-min>{{ filter.min_value.value | default: 0 | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
            <span data-xd-price-max>{{ filter.max_value.value | default: filter.range_max | money_without_trailing_zeros }}</span>
          </div>
          {%- comment -%}
            Shopify states money in cents; the slider works in whole currency
            units, so both ends are divided by 100 here and multiplied back in
            the JS label.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <span class="multi-range">
            <input
              type="range"
              min="0"
              max="{{ filter.range_max | divided_by: 100 }}"
              value="{{ filter.min_value.value | default: 0 | divided_by: 100 }}"
              id="lower"
              name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}"
              form="XdFacetForm"
              data-xd-price
            >
            <input
              type="range"
              min="0"
              max="{{ filter.range_max | divided_by: 100 }}"
              value="{{ filter.max_value.value | default: filter.range_max | divided_by: 100 }}"
              id="upper"
              name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}"
              form="XdFacetForm"
              data-xd-price
            >
          </span>
        </div>

      {%- when 'swatch' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Colour chips.

          The design ships an exact class per colour (.color-charcoal,
          .color-navy, .color-crimson, .color-ivory in main.css), so the value's
          handle is emitted as a class and those win when they exist. Any colour
          without a design class falls back to the swatch Shopify serves, and
          failing that to a neutral chip - so a new colour added in the admin
          still renders something sensible.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="accordion-body ps-3">
          <div class="d-flex gap-3 flex-wrap">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign label = value.label
                assign in_group = true
                if prefix != blank
                  assign value_prefix = label | split: separator | first
                  if value_prefix == prefix
                    assign label = label | remove_first: prefix | remove_first: separator
                  else
                    assign in_group = false
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              {%- if in_group -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign input_id = panel_id | append: '-' | append: forloop.index
                  assign colour_handle = label | handleize
                  assign colour_class = colour_handle | prepend: 'color-'

                  # An inline style would outrank the design's class, so it is
                  # only emitted for colours the design does not already paint.
                  assign chip = ''
                  unless design_colour_list contains colour_handle
                    if value.swatch.image
                      assign chip_image = value.swatch.image | image_url: width: 100
                      capture chip
                        echo 'background-image:url(' | append: chip_image | append: ');background-size:cover;background-position:center;'
                      endcapture
                    elsif value.swatch.color
                      capture chip
                        echo 'background-color:rgb(' | append: value.swatch.color.rgb | append: ');'
                      endcapture
                    endif
                  endunless
                -%}
                <div class="color-option">
                  <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    class="color-checkbox"
                    id="{{ input_id }}"
                    form="XdFacetForm"
                    name="{{ value.param_name }}"
                    value="{{ value.value | escape }}"
                    data-xd-facet-input
                    data-xd-count="{{ value.count }}"
                    {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                    {% if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %}disabled{% endif %}
                  >
                  <label
                    for="{{ input_id }}"
                    class="fbf-color__opt {{ colour_class }}{% if chip == blank %} fbf-color__opt--blank{% endif %}"
                    {% if chip != blank %}style="{{ chip }}"{% endif %}
                    title="{{ label | escape }}"
                  >
                    <span class="visually-hidden">
                      {{- label | escape }} (<span data-xd-count-text>{{ value.count }}</span>)
                    </span>
                  </label>
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>

      {%- when 'rating' -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          Star rows. The value label is a number once the prefix is off
          ("Rating: 4" -> "4"), so it is drawn as full/half/empty stars; if
          something non-numeric arrives the label is printed as-is.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <div class="accordion-body ps-3">
          <div class="product-review">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign label = value.label
                assign in_group = true
                if prefix != blank
                  assign value_prefix = label | split: separator | first
                  if value_prefix == prefix
                    assign label = label | remove_first: prefix | remove_first: separator
                  else
                    assign in_group = false
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              {%- if in_group -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign input_id = panel_id | append: '-' | append: forloop.index
                  assign score = label | times: 1.0
                  assign full_stars = score | floor
                  assign has_half = false
                  assign fraction = score | minus: full_stars
                  if fraction >= 0.5
                    assign has_half = true
                  endif
                  assign half_index = full_stars | plus: 1
                -%}
                <label class="review-star d-block{% if value.active %} is-active{% endif %}" for="{{ input_id }}">
                  <input
                    type="checkbox"
                    class="visually-hidden"
                    id="{{ input_id }}"
                    form="XdFacetForm"
                    name="{{ value.param_name }}"
                    value="{{ value.value | escape }}"
                    data-xd-facet-input
                    data-xd-count="{{ value.count }}"
                    {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                    {% if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %}disabled{% endif %}
                  >
                  {%- if score > 0 -%}
                    {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                      {%- if i <= full_stars -%}
                        <i class="fa-sharp fa-solid fa-star" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      {%- elsif i == half_index and has_half -%}
                        <i class="fa-duotone fa-sharp fa-solid fa-star-half" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      {%- else -%}
                        <i class="fa-sharp fa-regular fa-star" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endfor %}
                    <strong class="d-inline-block ms-2">{{ rating_suffix }}</strong>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <strong class="d-inline-block">{{ label | escape }}</strong>
                  {%- endif -%}
                  {%- if show_count -%}
                    <span class="ms-1">(<span data-xd-count-text>{{ value.count }}</span>)</span>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </label>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </div>
        </div>

      {%- else -%}
        <div class="accordion-body ps-3">
          <ul class="list-unstyled m-0">
            {%- for value in filter.values -%}
              {%- liquid
                assign label = value.label
                assign in_group = true
                if prefix != blank
                  assign value_prefix = label | split: separator | first
                  if value_prefix == prefix
                    assign label = label | remove_first: prefix | remove_first: separator
                  else
                    assign in_group = false
                  endif
                endif
              -%}
              {%- if in_group -%}
                {%- assign input_id = panel_id | append: '-' | append: forloop.index -%}
                <li class="mb-2">
                  <div class="form-check">
                    <input
                      class="form-check-input"
                      type="checkbox"
                      id="{{ input_id }}"
                      form="XdFacetForm"
                      name="{{ value.param_name }}"
                      value="{{ value.value | escape }}"
                      data-xd-facet-input
                      data-xd-count="{{ value.count }}"
                      {% if value.active %}checked{% endif %}
                      {% if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %}disabled{% endif %}
                    >
                    {%- comment -%}
                      The design only lays a label out as a spread row when it
                      carries a count (listing.html "Category"); plain checkbox
                      rows are a bare .form-check-label.filter-link.
                    {%- endcomment -%}
                    <label class="form-check-label filter-link{% if show_count %} d-flex justify-content-between align-items-center w-100{% endif %}" for="{{ input_id }}">
                      {{ label | escape }}
                      {%- if show_count -%}
                        <span data-xd-count-text>{{ value.count }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </label>
                  </div>
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ul>
        </div>
    {%- endcase -%}
  </div>
</div>
